  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "A clear workspace for the next repair",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"A clear workspace for the next repair\"**\n\nThe public site presents a practical desktop product with generous spacing, calm near-black surfaces and a warm gold identity. The user's pinned reference, Cerberus Tool Pro, informs capsule navigation, the paired hero and contrasting annual card. ArepaTool content, colors and assets remain authoritative.\n\nDirection contract: TYPE is Geist with strong scale and moderate weights; MATERIAL is existing logo/mascot artwork and an illustrative workspace; GROUND is black with restrained gold; FORM follows the pinned reference, taking precedence over exploratory seed 0659cdb2; the quality target is its clarity, spacing and pricing hierarchy rather than its brand treatment.\n\nThe approved landing composition and its guidance below remain intact. The same pinned world extends across secondary public pages, authentication, user accounts, administration and reseller tools. Operational surfaces use denser layouts without changing copy or workflows. Source evidence: `src/styles/application.css`, `auth.css`, `dashboard.css`, `admin.css` and `public-interior.css`.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Large, restrained sans-serif headings.",
      "Tonal dark surfaces with gold actions.",
      "Clearly separated license and credit offers.",
      "An interactive, explicitly illustrative module preview."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "Scope",
        "body": "Apply the shared black/gold identity to the entire website: landing and public interior pages, authentication, user, admin and reseller interfaces. Keep the marketing layout flag and app/interior selectors as styling boundaries; they do not exclude private screens from the refresh or change access permissions.",
        "section": "Colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "Hierarchy",
        "body": "Use size and spacing before extra decoration. Preserve readable technical names and localized content in ES, EN and PT-BR.",
        "section": "Typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "Clear Controls",
        "body": "At widths up to 799px, WhatsApp and the update reopening button live in document flow below the footer so they cannot cover content. Desktop retains corner shortcuts.",
        "section": "Layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "Containment",
        "body": "Keep wide tables and logs inside their own keyboard-scrollable regions, never the page viewport. Preserve columns, record values and actions; wrap long identifiers and translated labels rather than dropping data. Component height tokens describe current heights/minima; allow labels to wrap and retain larger controls in auth/mobile contexts.",
        "section": "Layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "Preservation",
        "body": "This is a visual refresh only. Original copy in every locale, authentication/authorization, routes, API behavior, prices and pricing logic, balances, licensing and reseller operations remain unchanged.",
        "section": "Components"
      },
      {
        "name": "Access",
        "body": "Preserve focus rings, the skip link, translated control labels and reduced-motion support. Check mobile overflow after content changes.",
        "section": "Components"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** preserve real prices, reseller contacts and release content.",
      "**Do** optimize existing artwork without changing its identity.",
      "**Do** keep public presentation separate from billing and account behavior.",
      "**Do** check desktop, mobile and all three languages."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** present the preview as a live connected device.",
      "**Don't** invent statistics, reviews or popularity claims.",
      "**Don't** cover mobile controls with floating shortcuts.",
      "**Don't** apply the FOXUNLOCKERS fire exception to ordinary cards."
    ]
  }
}
